Subject: [PATCH 3/9] geph5-app: add the `register` subcommand

Declaring the enum variant is the whole of this patch; the implementation is
patch 4. Kept separate so that a conflict in the handler body cannot cost you
the CLI surface, which is what the module's shell scripts actually parse.

Deriving the variant name from the keyword gives the `geph5 register` verb.

---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/binaries/geph5-app/src/cli.rs b/binaries/geph5-app/src/cli.rs
index e790a30..e3ffa03 100644
--- a/binaries/geph5-app/src/cli.rs
+++ b/binaries/geph5-app/src/cli.rs
@@ -36,6 +36,9 @@ pub enum Command {
     Logout,
     /// Show account information.
     Account,
+    /// Register a new free account by solving a proof-of-work puzzle, then
+    /// log in with the resulting secret.
+    Register,
 
     /// Bring the tunnel up.
     Connect,
